   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the education law, in relation to authorizing the retention of\nfederal funds for special education programs for preschool children",
    "basePrintNo": "S7096",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7096-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §4405, Ed L",
    "lawSection": "Education Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7096\n\nSPONSOR: COONEY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the education law, in relation to authorizing the\nretention of federal funds for special education programs for preschool\nchildren\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis bill includes programs covered under section 4410 to utilize feder-\nal funds, allowing federal funds to be used for special education\nprograms for preschool children.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of this bill provides that programs approved pursuant to\nsection forty-four hundred ten are eligible to retain funds in excess of\ntheir allowable and reimbursable costs incurred for services and\nprograms provided to school-age and preschool students.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nSpecial education programs that service preschool children are incredi-\nbly important, and have been previously overlooked by this section of\neducation law. Providing these programs access to federal funds will\nprovide equity for preschool-aged children.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately, with provisions.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
